            <ArticleTitle>Radiation-induced coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>239-44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes three patients who developed myocardial infarction at an untimely age, 4 to 12 years after radiation therapy for Hodgkin's disease. These cases lend credence to the cause and effect relation of such therapy to coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
